WEBVTT

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.690
Coucou! Moyashimon here!

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:06.120
We're coming at you from 
France again this week!

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.340
Last time, Ryuuta tried 
everything he could think of

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:13.050
to try to win Hasegawa's heart 
and get her to marry him.

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:16.530
But, determined to stop him, 
Tadayasu, Misato, and Kawahama

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:19.470
jumped into the middle and 
turned the situation around.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.910
The party arranged for 
Hasegawa was ruined,

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.430
and Ryuuta was enraged, 
convinced that even

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.260
Hasegawa had made a fool of him.

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:29.950
Where's Haruka?

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.510
She has returned to the room.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:35.630
What? Didn't you tell her I was here?

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.660
Yes, I told her,

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.640
but she seems to be 
quite tired as well.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.340
That woman...

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.270
Maybe I should let her 
have it, just once.

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.480
Haruka! Give it a rest or...

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:54.490
I-Is that the wine that was in the car?

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.990
So you're going to marry me, eh?

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:04.500
Hey... don't you find 
blood incredibly sexy?

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:07.000
Haruka-san?

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:17.470
Moyashimon

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:17.470
Returns

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:48.930
I can't remember anything...

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.070
G-Good morning! I'm sorry!

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.780
L-Look, after I shower,

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.820
I want to go to Beaune's morning market.

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:02.480
You should go.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.480
Yes, good idea! I'm sorry!

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:07.300
May I join you after 
I've slept for a bit?

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.230
I'm sorry!

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:10.350
If I told you to finish

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:12.830
your sentences with that, you can stop.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.210
I'm sorry

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:15.950
Run! Run!

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:17.710
Marie! Don't run away 
before we can talk!

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:21.760
We're going to stay in 
Beaune and meet Hasegawa.

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.350
Sawaki, you wait at 
the base with Marie.

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:26.660
By "base," do you mean my house?

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:28.550
I'm worried.

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:32.100
You two better not just borrow 
money from Hasegawa-san.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.170
Oh, come on.

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.900
Hasegawa wanted to 
apologize to Marie, too.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.730
We intend to bring her back.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:39.980
I don't want to.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:41.880
There's no point in seeing her now.

00:03:41.880 --> 00:03:43.360
Now, don't say that...

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.110
Anyway, we're going to beat it for now.

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:48.010
If the bike rental guy shows 
up, we're in trouble.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:48.870
Right!

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:53.550
I guess I should be glad 
I got to come out alone.

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:54.960
Miss...

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:58.000
Unfortunately, it is likely your

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.360
freedom will come to 
an end this afternoon.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:00.960
Huh?

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:02.990
I received word

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:06.100
from the Paris branch that several 
people will be sent here.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:09.410
I will accompany them in 
assisting Ryuuta-san,

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:11.170
and I have been ordered 
not to let you leave

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:13.270
Ryuuta-san's side in the meantime.

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:15.090
My father again, huh?

00:04:15.090 --> 00:04:17.480
Were you really supposed 
to tell me that?

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:20.730
No, I wasn't. It will be our secret.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:27.080
No matter where I go or what I do,

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:29.100
I'm still just a bird in a cage.

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:38.230
Did you know that grape leaves 
change colors in autumn?

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:41.590
This has been my favorite season 
ever since I was little.

00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:46.650
Pretty soon, all these Pinot 
Noir will turn yellow and red

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:48.470
as far as the eye can see,

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:51.170
and Côte-d'Or will be 
painted in gold.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:53.690
I like fall, too.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:56.820
My household and my 
friend's family's brewery

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:59.070
are filled with the smell 
of the malt fungi.

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:02.410
When I was little,

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:05.410
I hated it because all my 
classmates said it stunk,

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:07.800
but when fall came and 
I could smell it again,

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.270
it relaxed me somehow.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:10.990
Our winery will be

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:14.010
shrouded in the smell of 
fermenting grapes soon, too.

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:16.660
I can't say I dislike it.

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:19.250
Actually, I love it.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:25.310
Then why don't you want to 
take over the business?

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:33.690
Good morning, Marie.

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:34.600
Morning.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:35.600
Bonjour!

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:37.740
You're out early, Dad.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:39.720
We're going out to pull 
up the old roots.

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:41.610
I thought I should learn 
the ropes from Grandpa.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:43.670
Oh? Well, good luck.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:45.040
Let's head back.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:46.400
We need to eat breakfast.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:47.110
Huh?

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:00.130
Beaune Morning Market

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:04.730
So, I'm running away.

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:05.780
Take me with you.

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:08.380
Why are you always so high-and-mighty?

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:10.890
That's not how a bride is 
supposed to be taken away.

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:13.250
Whatever. I don't have time.

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:17.270
My father might already have 
people on watch in this town.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:21.850
Which means taking off in the 
car right now is a bad idea.

00:06:21.850 --> 00:06:24.530
If only we could disguise you...

00:06:25.060 --> 00:06:25.780
Disguise?

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:29.060
We do have some things.

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:33.800
I'm going to move away a bit,

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:35.590
so it won't look unnatural.

00:06:35.590 --> 00:06:37.390
Hurry up! Let's go!

00:06:39.340 --> 00:06:41.040
Lend me your sombrero!

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:43.090
This is my soul.

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:45.050
I can't lend you my soul.

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:52.090
Come on, Haruka, don't be shy.

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:54.180
Say hello to Ryuuta-kun.

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:57.570
Ryuuta, you're older,

00:06:57.570 --> 00:07:00.010
so be sure you escort 
Haruka-chan properly.

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:00.810
Okay...

00:07:02.570 --> 00:07:04.320
W-Want to go play outside?

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:10.900
What an adorable couple.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:13.570
Master Ryuuta, you already 
have a girlfriend?

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.210
Can you climb trees?

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:21.580
I can, but not with these shoes on.

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:24.730
Could you if you took them off?

00:07:24.730 --> 00:07:25.590
What?

00:07:25.780 --> 00:07:28.520
I-I can, but not today.

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:30.090
My socks will get dirty.

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:32.640
Hey, there's a pond over there.

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:33.840
Let's go see the fish.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:38.560
Climb it next time.

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:43.080
Ryuuta-san! Ryuuta-san!

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.110
Pull yourself together, Ryuuta-san.

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:49.450
All we can do is support you.

00:07:49.450 --> 00:07:51.860
The only one who can 
pull it off is you.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:53.930
I know that.

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:55.620
Why are there so many of you here?

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:57.120
Beaune!

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:00.120
Okay, that takes care of our meal.

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:03.250
They've probably got someone 
at the station, too.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:04.610
I'll get on the train alone

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:07.130
and ride from Nuits-St.-Georges 
to Marie's house.

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:09.600
And what do we do?

00:08:09.600 --> 00:08:11.470
Marie and I will come 
back with her car,

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:13.630
so just try to escape out of town.

00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:14.990
If it looks like you won't make it,

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:17.390
head for Marie's village 
through the vineyards.

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:20.000
Take the route we used 
on the bike yesterday.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.230
You remember it, right?

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:21.890
Yeah.

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:24.700
Well then, from now on...

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:27.220
you two are a somewhat 
painfully matched couple.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:28.840
Don't remind us!

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:30.650
I told you, lend me your sombrero!

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:33.970
And I told you, 
I can't lend you my soul.

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:35.490
Make sure you give them the slip.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:36.710
Adios!

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:42.840
No matter how you look at it,

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:44.290
eating that meal only wasted time!

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:47.040
So, what do we do? Leave town?

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:50.920
And wasn't Marie-san's house 
out past Clos de Vougeot?

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:51.940
That's so far away.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:54.660
I guess we have no choice 
until we get there.

00:08:55.590 --> 00:08:58.090
I'll act like your 
girlfriend as we walk.

00:08:58.090 --> 00:08:59.770
G-Got it.

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:01.810
Then...

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:06.310
Wh-What?!

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:09.460
C-Couples walk hand in hand, right?

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:12.820
That's the only thing 
I know about couples!

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:22.450
Yeah... I guess couples 
do walk hand in hand.

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:24.920
If you get it, then walk faster!

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:26.710
We make a weird couple right now!

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:28.130
Y-Yeah...

00:09:28.130 --> 00:09:29.610
But you're going too fast.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:30.950
I'm wearing heels.

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:31.840
Oh...

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:36.020
Sorry.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:38.600
It's okay.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.220
Let's go.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:47.230
I'm terribly sorry, I lost Miss Haruka.

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:50.760
Find her!

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:52.700
Send a few people to 
Beaune Station by car!

00:09:52.700 --> 00:09:54.060
Everyone else head into town!

00:09:55.980 --> 00:09:57.270
Haruka-san...

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:03.620
Meanwhile, our main characters...

00:10:04.480 --> 00:10:07.160
The next 13 vines after 
number 23 are old,

00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:08.400
but they're healthy.

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:10.590
They're fine with a little pruning.

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:12.610
This is the last year for everything 
to this side of those.

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:16.340
Do you really have the details 
of all those vines memorized?

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:17.550
Well, yeah.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:19.840
It's expected of any Burgundy winemaker.

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:21.830
Bravo, Marie!

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:26.850
Don't you really want to go back 
and help with the wine making?

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:29.730
Who wants that? I'm just hungry!

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:37.050
Are you Japanese?

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:38.900
Have you seen this woman?

00:10:39.210 --> 00:10:40.910
No, I'm Mexican.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:43.910
Damn, so he really was Mexican.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:47.790
Whew, that was close.

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:50.330
I wonder if those two 
are out of town by now.

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:53.590
Surely they're not really 
acting like a couple.

00:10:58.270 --> 00:10:59.890
I swiped some of our stock.

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:01.530
Is that your dad's wine?

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:03.550
Yeah. Let's go eat.

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:06.040
Hey, bro!

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:08.310
We're this winery's cellar yeasts.

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:10.570
Would you tell Marie or her grandpa

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:12.910
to come look at the fermentation tank?

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:15.070
It feels colder than usual.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:18.070
Why? Isn't her father doing a good job?

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:20.290
Wow, he can talk to us!

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:22.810
I had a feeling he could. 
That's why I called to him.

00:11:22.810 --> 00:11:26.190
So, I don't want to say too 
much, but he's just a novice.

00:11:26.190 --> 00:11:28.640
Yeah, he doesn't understand us as well

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:30.080
as Marie or Grandpa do.

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:34.330
Even you'll do. Come to the winery!

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:36.590
You think I'm any better? 
I'm a novice, too!

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:38.510
But it's so cold!

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:41.390
Please, open the door 
or window or something!

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:42.500
Please?

00:11:41.390 --> 00:11:44.350
Hey, want to eat on the terrace?

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:47.550
Hey, I know this is out of nowhere,

00:11:47.550 --> 00:11:48.970
but could we go see the winery?

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.480
We can't. I don't go in there anymore.

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:58.910
How many bottles are you 
gonna drink this early?

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:00.990
Don't underestimate Westerners.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:03.060
Two bottles of wine is just a warm-up.

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:03.990
You gotta be kidding...

00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:08.990
Hey... do you think I 
was harsh to my dad?

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:12.220
No, I didn't really think that,

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:14.170
but I did kind of wonder why you

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:17.500
wouldn't go help him, 
when you love wine so much.

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:19.460
Our relationship isn't bad.

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:22.040
It's just not good, either.

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:26.320
Come on. I can show you the cave.

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:34.520
Marie!

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:37.020
Wow... there's blue mold everywhere.

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:39.710
The mold in a cave makes 
a bed for the wine.

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:42.830
Being gently enveloped in mold

00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:45.140
is the prime condition for aging.

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:47.830
This is also my study room.

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:49.030
Only in summer, though.

00:12:49.030 --> 00:12:50.630
You're drinking again?

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:51.540
Of course.

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:53.540
And while I'm here, I should

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.920
check Dad's replanting schedule.

00:12:57.770 --> 00:12:59.420
That seems really unnatural.

00:12:59.990 --> 00:13:02.320
You really want to help him, don't you?

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:03.420
Oh, shut up.

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:07.020
It's not that I don't 
get along with my dad.

00:13:07.020 --> 00:13:09.430
But my brother and I grew 
up around our grandpa.

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:13.180
Ever since I was little, I'd go 
out into the vineyards every day,

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:15.190
so I know everything about them.

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:17.350
My dad, on the other hand,

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:19.320
was a businessman in the city.

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:21.690
He only took over the vineyard 
because work wasn't going well.

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:24.890
But our buyers and everyone in the village

00:13:24.890 --> 00:13:29.200
had high hopes for my brother and me.

00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:31.970
Maybe that made Dad feel inferior.

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:34.790
One day, he declared 
that he would refuse

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:36.270
all help from both of us.

00:13:37.150 --> 00:13:39.350
We didn't mind at all.

00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:41.210
We love our dad's pride.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:43.710
But why is that a reason to leave home?

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:46.720
From an outsider's perspective, 
it looks like you're quarreling.

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:50.110
But I'm really not leaving 
because we had a fight.

00:13:50.110 --> 00:13:52.780
Well, I did decide to 
leave because of Dad...

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:54.870
But that's part of why

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:56.810
I want to see the outside world, too.

00:13:57.660 --> 00:14:00.720
You know everything 
about all the vines.

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:03.360
I would think that'd be 
a huge help to your dad.

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:05.370
But it was Dad who decided

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:09.650
that he would be Grandpa's 
legitimate successor.

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:12.620
It's only logical for the rest 
of our family to support him.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.080
Is it...

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.360
It is!

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:17.430
Besides, my mom has her own business,

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:18.840
a restaurant in Paris.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:22.590
My Mom gives my dad's wine 
priority at that restaurant.

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:25.510
The whole family is supporting my dad!

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:27.300
I get it, it's just...

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.160
What is it that doesn't 
feel right here?

00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:30.930
Oh, yeah.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:33.890
The cellar yeasts here were 
asking for your help, at least.

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:34.890
What?

00:14:35.450 --> 00:14:40.080
Which probably means that you 
should just help your dad.

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:42.180
But then everyone in the village

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:44.900
would look at it as your 
work, not your dad's...

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:46.500
Ah, what the hell?

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:49.030
I guess rural life sucks no 
matter what country you live in.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:50.030
Shut up!

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:51.460
Someone who's content to be a successor

00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:53.570
has no right to talk 
about other households!

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:57.040
No cabs are coming.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.600
Forget this.

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:00.850
Let's just start walking to Marie's.

00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:04.230
Yeah. It's been a while 
since Kawahama left.

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:05.800
He might be headed this way.

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:08.170
Crap! I missed my stop!

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:11.050
Okay, that's enough for today.

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:19.180
Huh? Was I sitting at 
this desk for that long?

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:22.480
We're looking for a Japanese woman who

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.690
visited this property yesterday evening.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.690
The sun's already setting?

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:27.190
I haven't seen her today.

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:28.380
That's enough!

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:30.390
I'm going to wait back at the hotel!

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:32.450
You guys keep looking for Haruka!

00:15:37.030 --> 00:15:41.000
Marie, will your guests be 
returning by dinnertime?

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.840
I think they might bring back one more.

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:46.170
If all goes well, we might all 
have Cros Parantoux tonight.

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:49.500
That was close!

00:15:49.500 --> 00:15:51.850
But if they came all this 
way looking for her,

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:54.350
that must mean the plan worked.

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:57.350
Hey, why are you alone?

00:15:57.830 --> 00:16:00.790
What is that phony Mexican doing?!

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:02.850
There aren't even any 
street lights out here!

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:04.860
Once night falls, we won't 
be able to see the road!

00:16:05.510 --> 00:16:07.710
Um... we don't have to hold 
hands anymore, do we?

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:08.860
O-Oh, yeah...

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:11.380
Also, I'm exhausted.

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:12.860
Let's sit down for a bit.

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:15.110
I'm actually glad these 
are vineyard paths.

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:17.110
I wonder how far I've 
walked in these heels...

00:16:17.110 --> 00:16:18.320
Pretty far.

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:20.370
Anyway, if you think about 
it, this is just weird.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:23.430
If I'm getting married, 
why isn't my father here?

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:26.130
Well, we only heard it 
secondhand ourselves...

00:16:26.410 --> 00:16:30.130
Still, I wouldn't put it past 
him and Ryuuta to do that.

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:32.630
Force you to get married, you mean?

00:16:33.320 --> 00:16:36.230
Our fathers are old work buddies.

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:38.220
Since I was little,

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:41.150
every time he dragged me 
to a meeting or party,

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:43.640
he always made me hang out with Ryuuta.

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:47.390
Part of it was that he was the 
only other kid close to my age,

00:16:47.390 --> 00:16:51.650
but I guess he might have also 
felt some duty to protect me.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:56.160
I wanted him to climb trees with me.

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:57.530
Huh? Trees?

00:17:00.530 --> 00:17:01.910
Can you climb trees?

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:06.330
I can, but not with these shoes on.

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:10.780
My father scolded me after that.

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:14.260
He asked me, "what if 
Ryuuta-kun had gotten hurt?"

00:17:15.210 --> 00:17:16.740
He would never climb trees

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:19.890
with me after that, even in secret.

00:17:21.030 --> 00:17:24.950
And as all this went on, 
our fathers' imprinting continued.

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:28.690
Before I knew it, he was seriously 
calling me his fiancée, too.

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:32.510
I thought, once we grew 
up, I could refuse.

00:17:33.100 --> 00:17:35.110
So I guess all I can do is run,

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:37.190
even if they'll catch me right away.

00:17:39.170 --> 00:17:40.700
Wh-Wh-Wha—

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:57.220
Sorry! It looked like 
a fancy car, so...

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:59.720
Th-Then if you'd just said so, 
I would have hidden!

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:01.740
I-I'm sorry.

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:03.540
Forget it, just move.

00:18:05.200 --> 00:18:07.810
Also... I'm not really in a 
position to say it, but...

00:18:08.400 --> 00:18:09.310
Look.

00:18:17.130 --> 00:18:19.550
Wow! I don't think I've 
ever seen so many stars!

00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:22.130
So you can see all this

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:23.910
when there are no lights 
and the air's clean...

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:28.630
Do you know the Summer Triangle?

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:29.630
Yeah...

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:31.790
But it's fall. Is it visible now?

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:33.150
Oh...

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:34.780
Isn't there a winter one, too?

00:18:34.780 --> 00:18:36.250
What was it called again?

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:38.250
Then, did you know that the

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:40.550
North Star isn't always the same star?

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:46.830
Are you trying to cheer me up?

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:51.560
I-If you don't want to do it, 
I agree that you could run away.

00:18:51.800 --> 00:18:55.950
But... it would be tough, 
suddenly not having you around.

00:18:57.500 --> 00:18:58.570
I guess so.

00:18:59.140 --> 00:19:02.140
Everyone's out looking for you 
and trying to bring you back

00:19:02.140 --> 00:19:03.950
because we all like you.

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:07.350
But, for now, putting 
the others aside...

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:09.560
Come back with us.

00:19:11.260 --> 00:19:12.110
Okay.

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:19.130
Hey, why do you know 
so much about stars?

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:21.230
Oh, you know. Here.

00:19:21.230 --> 00:19:22.050
Thanks.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:26.840
You shameless, bearded fool!

00:19:26.840 --> 00:19:28.300
What the hell?!

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:29.130
Shut up!

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:30.970
You're the ones appearing 
out of the dark together!

00:19:30.970 --> 00:19:32.360
Don't "What the hell" me!

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:36.600
You're doing this while we're 
busting our asses making plans?!

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:37.740
What?!

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:41.510
You've really got guts, 
offering Hasegawa your hand.

00:19:41.510 --> 00:19:44.910
But then, I've had my suspicions 
ever since the spring festival.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:47.300
Are you stupid?! 
Why don't you ask her?!

00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:49.650
You must be exhausted. Are you cold?

00:19:49.650 --> 00:19:51.860
What a crazy, messy day, huh?

00:19:51.860 --> 00:19:53.250
Messy is right.

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:54.430
We didn't do anything!

00:19:54.430 --> 00:19:56.540
Come on, Hasegawa, don't be so quiet!

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:58.760
Say something!

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:04.890
I'm not taking a bath tonight.

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:05.890
Huh?

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:06.970
Huh?

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:10.830
Today was fun.

00:20:10.830 --> 00:20:13.430
Misato! Just look what 
you made her say!

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:15.870
What?! Y-You've got it all wrong!

00:20:15.870 --> 00:20:19.300
Researcher Hasegawa!

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.950
Moyashimon

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.950
Returns

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:52.950
Episode 9

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.950
Microbe 
Theater

00:21:50.400 --> 00:21:52.950
Microbe Theater Returns!

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:52.950
Returns

00:21:53.320 --> 00:21:56.040
Wow... there's blue mold everywhere.

00:21:57.190 --> 00:21:59.960
He's right, there is 
blue mold everywhere.

00:21:57.290 --> 00:22:00.500
P. chrysogenum 
(blue mold)

00:21:59.960 --> 00:22:04.040
We blue molds aren't the 
only ones in this cave!

00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:07.840
[The French term for a wine storage cellar]

00:22:04.040 --> 00:22:06.930
There are lots of yeasts and 
lactic acid bacteria, too!

00:22:07.290 --> 00:22:10.220
Let's get all the yeasts in here first!

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:18.560
Yeasts

00:22:16.620 --> 00:22:18.560
T. delbrueckii                              M. pulcherrima                     C. tropicalis

00:22:16.620 --> 00:22:18.560
C. stellata                               Z. bailii                                 P. guilliermondii

00:22:16.620 --> 00:22:18.560
P. anomala                        S. pombe                         C. zeylanoides

00:22:17.020 --> 00:22:18.560
We're yeasts!

00:22:19.130 --> 00:22:21.950
Wow, there are so many different kinds!

00:22:21.950 --> 00:22:25.150
Next, let's get the 
lactic acid bacteria in here!

00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:26.900
L. brevis

00:22:26.900 --> 00:22:27.740
L. hilgardii

00:22:27.740 --> 00:22:28.740
L. plantarum

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:29.660
O. oeni

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:32.160
P. pentosaceus

00:22:30.550 --> 00:22:33.320
We're lactic acid bacteria!

00:22:33.320 --> 00:22:36.430
Hey! You're sake's 
natural enemy, hiochi!

00:22:36.430 --> 00:22:37.920
What are you doing here?!

00:22:39.090 --> 00:22:42.620
Here, I'm called L. fructivorans.

00:22:42.620 --> 00:22:45.160
Japanese sake brewers hate us,

00:22:43.750 --> 00:22:46.090
L. fructivorans 
(hiochi)

00:22:45.160 --> 00:22:47.880
but we're quite popular in wine making!
